<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Blue Star</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1984</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Blue Star was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a>'s assault in June 1984 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a> complex at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a>, the holiest shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikhism</a>, to remove the armed Sikh militant leader Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale and his followers. The fighting killed Bhindranwale and hundreds of others, including many pilgrims, and badly damaged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akal-takht">Akal Takht</a>. In October 1984 Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> was assassinated by two of her Sikh bodyguards in revenge.</p></div>
